# N2/P10 Results - Fused Minimal Telemetry Construction

## Status

P10 is complete. The frozen P8/P9 dispatch policy and P6 folding backend were held unchanged while P9's seven-counter telemetry was fused directly into one specialized source `Factory._make` path.

Mandatory invariance passed on all **332/332** frozen policy cases: 188 training, 98 validation, 36 Gate-P evaluation, and 10 natural evaluation cases. P10 reproduced P9's seven primitive counters, five tree inputs, frozen-tree prediction, and annotate/bypass decision exactly. Fresh fuzz passed **1000/1000**.

## Gate-P primary endpoint

| Comparison | Case-balanced geomean | 95% bootstrap CI | Workload-weighted | Wins |
|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|
| P10 / direct, source-inclusive | **1.067366x** | **0.996775-1.118040** | **1.028688x** | 2/36 |
| P10 / P9, source-inclusive | **0.976619x** | **0.969118-0.984328** | **0.976601x** | 30/36 |
| P10 / direct, source build | **1.520357x** | **1.483467-1.553044** | **1.535783x** | 0/36 |
| P10 / P9, source build | **0.934367x** | **0.927659-0.941463** | **0.931841x** | 36/36 |
| P10 / direct, selected compiler | **0.970169x** | **0.860653-1.050463** | **0.831443x** | 7/36 |

The preregistered **direct-crossover criterion failed**: P10 remained about **6.7% slower** than direct case-balanced, and its confidence interval includes 1. However, the gap fell from P9's simultaneous result: P10 was **2.3% faster than P9** source-inclusive, with the complete 95% interval below 1.

The narrower fused-construction engineering criterion also failed because P10/P9 source build was **0.9344x**, an improvement of about **6.6%**, short of the preregistered 10% target. The source-inclusive P10/P9 portion of that criterion did pass.

Median Gate-P source construction was approximately **47.0 us direct**, **79.2 us P9**, and **75.3 us P10**.

