## Dispatch and Boolean work

P10 made exactly the same frozen decisions as P9/P8: **5/36** Gate-P cases annotated, all **5** consuming a fold, for **5** total consumed folds. Relative to simultaneous always-P6 profitability, 3 annotations were P6 wins, 2 were P6 losses, and 4 P6-winning cases were bypassed.

Because the decisions are invariant, the Boolean-work reductions are the same selective P8/P9 mechanism:

- multiplications: **0.812451x direct**;
- pair terms: **0.570459x direct**;
- peak monomials: **0.978577x direct**;
- ANF nodes evaluated: **0.873553x direct**.

## Memory

Gate-P traced peak allocation was **1.011176x direct** and **1.002189x P9**. P10 therefore changes time more than memory; its data representation is intentionally the same as P9's.

## Natural EPFL control

P10 annotated **0/10** frozen natural cases and consumed **0 folds**. Natural results remain strictly an abstention/overhead control.

